    "recommendations": "Reducing the density of vegetation in direct contact with and immediately surrounding the structure could meaningfully improve defensible space and reduce fuel continuity near the building. Where tree clusters are present close to the structure, increasing the horizontal separation between tree canopies and maintaining vertical separation between ground-level vegetation and lower tree branches would help address ladder fuel concerns and may reduce opportunities for fire to move from surface fuels into the canopy. Managing dense shrub cover and scattered shrubs within the immediate structure perimeter by thinning or increasing spacing could further reduce fuel continuity across the property. The open green space on the property is a valuable asset and its continued maintenance would support suppression operations and provide beneficial separation from surrounding brushland. Ensuring the long driveway remains clear of encroaching vegetation along its edges and overhead would support firefighter access and improve evacuation route usability, which are among the most operationally important priorities for this property."
